A highly enchanted stack of 15-25 ya, once you've maxed luck, will
last for an absurdly long time.  FWIW, my last samurai enchanted 16-17
ya.  15 made it to the demigod bar.  Granted, they were reserved for
something extra nasty I don't want to (or shouldn't) melee.

> In other words, if I have to decide between enchanting a massive stack
> of regular arrows, or enchanting a small pile of ya arrows, then I'm
> going for the massive stack of regular arrows.

I think this depends on class.  A two-weaponing wombat with a pair of
highly enchanted melee weapons doesn't need a large stack of
missiles.  A small stack of the best available usually suffices.  For
classes that can't (or shouldn't) two-weapon (hea, ran, rog, wiz),
enchanting the larger stack usually the smarter move.

In either case, enchanting breakable ammunition before maximizing luck
is quite frustrating.  Early on, a samurai's +0 ya and a ranger's +2
foo-arrows should be used judiciously.

